{
  "notes": "T2 plan. Mari bought. Geometry: bought/free cities cannot hold troops, so the ONLY enemy access to my homeland is Ekallatum (adj Sippar, Durkurigalzu, Mari). An attacker from there has strength 1 (no supporter can stand next to Sippar/Durkurigalzu), so a held province bounces it; keep Sippar and Durkurigalzu manned. Babylon, Nippur, Ur are unreachable. Mari: Assyria can hit it from Terqa with Ekallatum support = 2; Sippar supporting Mari walls makes it 2 vs 2, a tie, so Mari holds. Keep Sippar on 'support mari' every season. Assyria took Terqa by force and refused to promise anything on Mari: it is aggressive, its words are cheap. It has about 3 armies for 6 provinces, so its provinces are thin. I decided to try Susa by force: Nippur -> Susa, supported by Durkurigalzu (2 vs walls 1; bounces if an Assyrian army in Arbela supports Susa). A bounce costs nothing. If it falls, my army holds it and Arbela (adj Susa) may be empty to walk into. I know I am breaking my spoken word to Artessupa; my envoy Tattamaru is in Assyria and may be detained. Bought Qadesh (300) first: Mitanni may afford it by T3, Alashiya by T4. Damascus (250) next turn; Alashiya may afford it at T3 so a collision is possible. Hired c17 as a third envoy: send him to Mitanni at T3 proposing a joint strike on Assyria (Terqa and Ashur to Mitanni; Susa, Ekallatum, Arbela to me). T3 TODO: read Tattamaru and Kidin-Adad reports; buy Damascus; consider an army at Ur or Nippur (100) if the Susa move bounced, to add a third supporter.",
