{
  "notes": "T6: Both envoys (c13, c14) are on the road home, so no letters can go this season. Treasury 150 (includes 25 from Arzawa, weighed true, not assayed). Forecast: T7 about 158 after back pay 42; with envoys away again, cash grows about 50 a season (their wages build as back pay instead), so Amurru (200) is affordable around T9; buy is scheduled T10 as a fallback. NEW DANGER: Egypt holds Tyre with an army and has a fleet in levantsea; army tyre->byblos supported by that fleet is strength 2 vs the walls 1, so Byblos can fall any season. My fleet cannot reach it (enkomi is not next to byblos) and must hold Enkomi, so I accept the risk. If Byblos falls I wake; then think about retaking it or a deal with Egypt. At T7: read Paser's Egypt answer and Ili-iddina's Arzawa answer; send them out again (Egypt: peace tablet, Byblos safe; Arzawa: seal the tablet without the ship clause; keep warning them about Hatti). Re-plan the schedule at T7 (buy Amurru at T8/T9 if cash allows). Stay neutral between Hatti and Arzawa; do not send my fleet to the Syrian Sea while Egypt's fleets sit in levantsea and greatgreen.",
  "summary": "T1: bought Byblos (300). T2: sealed k8 with Hatti (no army/fleet vs each other's lands or bought cities; Hatti may buy Carchemish, Isuwa, Lukka; I may buy Ugarit, Amurru, Byblos, Qadesh). Egypt tried to land at Tamassos in T2 and T3 and bounced off my fleet. T4: sealed k16 and k25 with Arzawa (peace; Arzawa holds Lukka, may buy Ugarit; I may buy Byblos, Amurru, Tyre, Gaza, Damascus; neither bids for the other's cities; envoys pass freely). T5: Egypt gave only warm words; Babylon's Tattamaru agreed in words that Amurru is mine, nothing sealed. T6: Egypt took Tyre (army from megiddo, fleet levantsea support). Arzawa bought Ugarit, holds Lukka, sent 25 gold and asked my fleet to guard Ugarit in the Syrian Sea against Hatti; I refused (fleet must hold Enkomi) and sealed nothing; Arzawa promised by word to warn me of Egypt/Hatti moves and not to bid for my cities. Hatti pleads drought and wants gold; I sent none. MAP: only Amurru is still a free city. Bought walled cities cannot hold troops and fall to a move with one support (2 v 1). Byblos is exposed to Egypt's army at Tyre plus fleet at levantsea; I cannot cover it. DEFENCE: fleet enkomi and army tamassos support each other holding (scheduled T6-T30). ECONOMY: income 115, upkeep 65, wages 21 (not paid in cash while envoys are away; back pay builds). A bought city returns 10 percent a season: buy Amurru (200) as soon as cash allows (T9ish; scheduled T10). Envoys c13 (8/season, term to T13) and c14 (13/season, term to T9: renew or lose him). Woken T7.",
