{
  "notes": "T8 plan. Strength 3323 (1.33), gold 304. Real growth needs conquest: each yield y gives +10y strength and +y gold a season. T8 orders explicit: damascus army -> qadesh (byblos army supports, 2 v walls 1); tyre -> damascus; gaza -> tyre; fleet levantsea -> enkomi with cilicia and syriansea fleets supporting (3 v army 1 + tamassos support 1 = 2). The old scheduled T8 fleet supports were mis-named, so I replaced every unit's T8 order. T9 schedule kept: qadesh army -> mari (damascus army supports; Babylon at sippar could support mari walls and tie, then just bounce, no loss); byblos army -> amurru (syriansea fleet supports); cilicia fleet -> tamassos (enkomi fleet supports); gaza-army on to byblos. T10 schedule: amurru army -> ugarit with syriansea fleet supporting. Decide ugarit at T10: Hatti asked me to stay out and has an army at kizzuwatna beside it; if I take it, keep fleet and army support. If T8 enkomi fails, fix T9 fleet orders. After the last conquest disband spare units (army 30, fleet 35) and bank gold; keep a fleet in each Cyprus city only if Arzawa or Hatti fleets threaten. Envoys: sent none, no gold; never seal anything naming Mari, Qadesh, Damascus, or Alashiya's tablet. c1 and c2 due back T9; c2 (Assyrian-born, owed 42) will probably leave: let him unless useful. Wake every turn (wake_in_turn 9).",
  "summary": "Egypt (Napkhururiya). Start strength 2500, treasury 600. T8: strength 3323 (1.33), gold 304, yield 310, income 310, upkeep 225 (4 armies, 3 fleets), wages 43. Conquest is my path; every free city is gone, targets are walled cities bought by others (Qadesh, Amurru, Mari: Babylon; Ugarit: Arzawa) and Alashiya's Enkomi and Tamassos. Conquered provinces stay mine without a garrison. Walls hold 1: mover plus one support wins 2 v 1, but another king's unit adjacent may support the walls and tie. Babylon cannot station troops in its walled cities and has no coast, so it cannot reach my northern provinces by land; Hatti (carchemish, kizzuwatna) and Arzawa (lukka, seha fleet) could. Held: akhetaten, byblos, damascus, delta, gaza, megiddo, memphis, sinai, thebes, tyre. Campaign: qadesh + enkomi T8; mari + amurru + tamassos T9; ugarit T10 (decide). Then disband spare units and bank gold; keep waking each turn. Treaties: k11 Assyria (friendship, receive envoys, join no enemy), k18 Hatti (peace, southern cities in Egypt's sphere), k19 Mitanni (same), k32 Mitanni brotherhood (word at once if a third king moves on a homeland; I sent 25 gold). Babylonia: nothing sealed, I refuse any tablet naming Mari, Qadesh, Damascus or Susa as theirs. Alashiya: never seal. People: c1 Mane (13, term T11, due T9), c2 Ashur-nadin (14, term T8, due T9, owed 42, may leave), c17 (16, term T8). Unassayed gold g2 (40 Babylonia) and g4 (20 Alashiya) not assayed.",
