  "summary": "Ashur-uballit of Assyria, start strength 1700 (yield 135), now about 681 (growth 0.40). T1 took Terqa, bought Susa; Babylon broke k2 at once. T4 k14/k23 with Mitanni, broken T5 (taidu->nineveh); Mitanni took Nineveh then Terqa (T7) and destroyed my Terqa army. T4 k27 with Egypt (friendship; promised gold never sent). T7 k44 with Hatti: stand together against Mitanni (Hatti: Carchemish, Isuwa, Harran; Assyria: Terqa, Taidu, Washukanni); Hatti will strike T11 (Washukanni/Taidu) and T12 (Harran), but its plan counts on my armies at Terqa/Nineveh which I no longer have. T8 Babylon took Ekallatum. I now hold only arbela and ashur (capital), one army each. Mitanni armies at nineveh, terqa; Babylon at ekallatum, susa, with sippar and durkurigalzu behind. Rules learned: dislodged unit is destroyed; failed move leaves unit at home with strength 1; support cut by any attack except from the province supported into; a unit that supports still holds at 1 plus hold-supports; attacking a supporter cuts its support. Babylon hits arbela from susa every season so arbela's hold-support is unreliable. Counter to terqa->ashur with nineveh support: attack nineveh from arbela. Treasury 0, cannot pay wages or scribes; c13 Ili-iddina is secretly in my pay in Babylon. Needs: peace with Mitanni or Babylon, or Hatti/Egypt help. c10 Yanhamu sent to Mitanni T9 (back T11); c16 Ammistamru due home T10 from Egypt.",
